; The build needs the build tools, and NODE_ENV decides otherwise.
;
; Render sets NODE_ENV=production in the environment, and npm reads that as
; "omit dev dependencies" — so `npm ci` installed 157 of 158 packages, left out
; @nestjs/cli, and the build died on `sh: 1: nest: not found`. Every tool this
; project compiles with — nest, tsc, prisma's CLI — is a devDependency, which is
; correct: none of them is loaded by the running server.
;
; `include` wins over `omit` in npm regardless of the order the two are given,
; so this holds whatever NODE_ENV says. It lives here rather than in a build
; command because a build command is settings on somebody's dashboard: it is
; invisible in review, absent from a new environment, and was the reason this
; failure took a deploy to discover.
;
; The cost is dev dependencies present on the running instance. They are inert —
; nothing in dist/ imports them — and that is a much smaller price than a build
; that cannot run.
include=dev
